<speak>
<p>Witness. Field Season One. Chapter One: Little Cow of the Upper Gulf.</p>
<break time="800ms"/>
<p>Vaquita means "little cow" in Spanish. An affectionate name, for an animal that has never asked for attention.</p>
<p>If you stood on the shore of the Upper Gulf of California at dawn, where the desert runs straight into a warm green sea, you would probably miss it. A small grey back. A ring-eyed face. One soft breath. Gone.</p>
<p>The smallest porpoise on Earth is also the shyest, and its entire world is that one corner of sea — the smallest range of any marine mammal. Most people who have fished those waters all their lives have never seen one.</p>
<p>This is the story of how a gentle animal nobody hunts became the rarest marine mammal alive. And why the people who know it best have not given up on it. By the end, you may not want to either.</p>
</speak>
